From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: 995 - resolve an MLO uplink by AP-MLD address

topology_build_tree_from_assoc() resolves a child s parent by feeding
node::upstream_bssid to cntlr_find_node_with_bssid(), which walks bss->bssid
only. That holds for a legacy backhaul, where the bSTA associates to one BSS.

An MLO bSTA associates to an AP-MLD, so upstream_bssid carries the MLD address,
and an MLD address is deliberately not the BSSID of any affiliated AP. The
lookup therefore never matches, every child is skipped, and the tree stays flat
with depth -1 for all nodes below the root.

Measured on the three-node mesh, 2026-07-28, after 990 let the bBSS fallback
populate upstream_bssid for the first time:

  al     depth  upstream_bssid
  86:f7    0    00:00:00:00:00:00
  ca:8e   -1    86:f7:56:41:01:d4   <- controller AP-MLD address
  e6:a9   -1    00:00:00:00:00:00

while the controller BSSIDs are 76:04:1c:81:bc:2f, 7e:04:1c:81:7c:2e and so on
- the address simply is not among them.

Fall back to a lookup over each node apmld_list when the BSS lookup misses.
Same class of defect as the ieee1905 origin bug fixed earlier the same day:
code written for one address layer being handed an address from another.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/topology.c
+++ b/src/topology.c
@@ -57,6 +57,33 @@
  * verified on HW: `ieee1905 info` shows only the controller as 8g's neighbor),
  * so that walk can never build the 2nd hop. n->upstream_bssid IS populated
  * 1-hop-reliably from Link Metric Responses, so chain child->parent by it. */
+/* An MLO bSTA associates to an AP-MLD, not to an individual BSS, so
+ * node::upstream_bssid carries the MLD address - which is deliberately not the
+ * BSSID of any affiliated AP. cntlr_find_node_with_bssid() walks bss->bssid
+ * only and therefore never resolves an MLO uplink.
+ *
+ * Measured on the three-node mesh 2026-07-28: 8g reported upstream_bssid
+ * 86:f7:56:41:01:d4, which is the controller AP-MLD address; the controller
+ * BSSIDs are 76:04:1c:81:bc:2f and friends. The lookup missed, the child was
+ * skipped, and depth stayed UNKNOWN for every node below the root.
+ */
+static struct node *find_node_with_mld_macaddr(struct controller *c,
+					       const uint8_t *macaddr)
+{
+	struct node *n = NULL;
+
+	list_for_each_entry(n, &c->agentlist, list) {
+		struct wifi_apmld_element *mld = NULL;
+
+		list_for_each_entry(mld, &n->apmld_list, list) {
+			if (!memcmp(mld->mld_macaddr, macaddr, 6))
+				return n;
+		}
+	}
+
+	return NULL;
+}
+
 void topology_build_tree_from_assoc(struct controller *c,
 				    struct bh_topology_data *topology,
 				    const uint8_t *ctrl_al_macaddr)
@@ -97,6 +124,8 @@
 				continue;
 			pn = cntlr_find_node_with_bssid(c, cn->upstream_bssid);
 			if (!pn)
+				pn = find_node_with_mld_macaddr(c, cn->upstream_bssid);
+			if (!pn)
 				continue;
 			pdev = topology_find_device(topology, pn->almacaddr);
 			if (!pdev || pdev->bh.depth == UNKNOWN_TREE_LEVEL)
